-- ============================================================================
-- H4 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Consequence Modelling, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/consequence/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: HOW MUCH GETS OUT AND WHERE DOES IT GO. Liquid outflow
-- through a hole by Bernoulli, with the static head and the pressure above the
-- liquid; gas outflow, choked at or below the critical pressure ratio and
-- subsonic above it, with a ratio exactly at the boundary counted as choked;
-- a pool on a bund floor or at a stated thickness, and a bund that overtops
-- refused; Mackay and Matsugu evaporation, taught as a single route
-- correlation; the Briggs rural sigmas by Pasquill-Gifford class; the
-- continuous Gaussian plume with ground reflection; ppm and mg/m3 at the
-- stated temperature; and the distance to a concentration with its three
-- states. Digest sections 1 to 13, and section 34.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A release from a height meets a
-- concentration twice, and the far root is the one beyond the peak. The
-- Associate capstone grades three outflows, a pool diameter, an off-axis
-- concentration and a far distance, and no heat flux, blast or probit.
-- ============================================================================

values ('consequence', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-consequence-model-computes","title":"What a Consequence Model Computes","lesson_keys":["l01-effects-before-frequencies","l02-every-input-carries-its-unit","l03-a-result-or-a-refusal","l04-the-sources-and-what-each-fixes","l05-the-refusals-by-name"]},{"key":"m02-liquid-through-a-hole","title":"Liquid Through a Hole","lesson_keys":["l01-bernoulli-through-a-hole","l02-static-head-and-ullage-pressure","l03-the-discharge-coefficient-and-the-hole","l04-when-nothing-flows-out"]},{"key":"m03-gas-through-a-hole","title":"Gas Through a Hole","lesson_keys":["l01-choked-and-subsonic","l02-the-critical-pressure-ratio","l03-the-choked-mass-rate","l04-the-subsonic-outflow-coefficient","l05-exactly-at-the-critical-ratio"]},{"key":"m04-pools-and-evaporation","title":"Pools and Evaporation","lesson_keys":["l01-a-pool-on-the-bund-floor","l02-a-pool-of-stated-thickness","l03-a-bund-that-overtops","l04-evaporation-by-mackay-and-matsugu"]},{"key":"m05-the-gaussian-plume","title":"The Gaussian Plume","lesson_keys":["l01-a-continuous-point-release","l02-stability-classes-and-the-briggs-sigmas","l03-reflection-at-the-ground","l04-ppm-and-milligrams-per-cubic-metre"]},{"key":"m06-how-far-the-plume-reaches","title":"How Far the Plume Reaches","lesson_keys":["l01-off-the-centreline-and-above-the-ground","l02-the-distance-to-a-concentration","l03-a-near-root-a-far-root-and-three-states","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
